[2026-09-16T15:45:34] Q080: Tell me about Anthony Minghella — what did he win and what happened at the Oscars after his death?
{"id": "Q080", "question": "Tell me about Anthony Minghella — what did he win and what happened at the Oscars after his death?", "information_need": "overview", "motivation": "intrinsic_learning", "prior_familiarity": "unfamiliar", "scope": "multi_document", "answerable": true, "adversarial_kind": null, "required_sources": ["Anthony_Minghella.html", "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html"], "expected_sources": ["Anthony_Minghella.html", "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html"], "retrieved_sources": ["Anthony_Minghella.html", "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "Brendan_Fraser.html"], "required_aspects": ["Anthony Minghella (1954–2008) was a British playwright and filmmaker who directed Truly, Madly, Deeply, The English Patient, The Talented Mr.", "Ripley and Cold Mountain.", "He won the Academy Award for Best Director for The English Patient, and received three further nominations: Best Adapted Screenplay for both The English Patient and The Talented Mr.", "Ripley, and, posthumously, Best Picture for The Reader (2008) as a producer.", "The Academy made an exception to its normal three-producer limit for Best Picture so that Minghella and Sydney Pollack could be posthumously included among the four producers nominated for The Reader."], "response": "Anthony Minghella was a British playwright and filmmaker, and he won the Academy Award for Best Director for *The English Patient* [Anthony_Minghella.html]. He also received Best Adapted Screenplay nominations for *The English Patient* and *The Talented Mr. Ripley*, and was posthumously nominated for Best Picture for *The Reader* as a producer [Anthony_Minghella.html].\n\nAfter his death, the Academy made an exception to its producer limit so that Anthony Minghella and Sydney Pollack were posthumously included among the four producers nominated for *The Reader* [Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html]. The *Best Picture* award is given to the film’s producers [Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html].", "closed_book_response": "Anthony Minghella was a British film director, writer, and producer best known for films like *The English Patient*, *Truly, Madly, Deeply*, *The Talented Mr. Ripley*, and *Cold Mountain*.\n\nWhat he won:\n- He won the Academy Award for Best Director for *The English Patient*.\n- He also won the BAFTA Award for Best Film for *The English Patient* as a producer.\n- *The English Patient* itself won a lot of Oscars, and Minghella was one of the key figures behind it.\n\nWhat happened at the Oscars after his death:\n- Anthony Minghella died in 2008, shortly before the Academy Awards that year.\n- At the Oscars, he was included in the annual tribute to people from the film industry who had died that year, the “In Memoriam” segment.\n- His death was also noted with respect by the Academy, reflecting his major contribution to film.\n\nIf you want, I can also give you a quick list of his most important films and awards.", "correctness": "pass", "graded_correctness": "complete", "graded_correctness_score": 1.0, "covered_aspects": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5], "aspect_coverage": 1.0, "answer_relevance": "pass", "claims": [{"text": "Anthony Minghella was a British playwright and filmmaker.", "cited_source": "Anthony_Minghella.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "He won the Academy Award for Best Director for *The English Patient*.", "cited_source": "Anthony_Minghella.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "He received Best Adapted Screenplay nominations for *The English Patient* and *The Talented Mr. Ripley*.", "cited_source": "Anthony_Minghella.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "He was posthumously nominated for Best Picture for *The Reader* as a producer.", "cited_source": "Anthony_Minghella.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "After his death, the Academy made an exception to its producer limit for *The Reader*.", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "Anthony Minghella and Sydney Pollack were posthumously included among the four producers nominated for *The Reader*.", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "The Best Picture award is given to the film’s producers.", "cited_source": "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}], "claim_count": 7, "graded_groundedness_score": 1.0, "faithfulness": "pass", "citation_support_rate": 1.0, "chunk_attribution_score": 0.5714285714285714, "source_hit_at_k": 1, "source_recall_at_k": 1.0, "source_precision_at_k": 0.6666666666666666, "source_recall_strict": 1.0, "all_required_present": true, "response_quote_count": 0, "quote_fidelity_rate": null, "quote_attribution_accuracy": null, "citation_count": 2, "citation_precision": 1.0, "unsupported_citation_rate": 0.0, "refusal_outcome": "n/a", "answer_latency_seconds": 1.8778205000271555, "judge_latency_seconds": 5.97215449999203, "total_latency_seconds": 11.492114800028503, "input_tokens": 101802, "output_tokens": 814, "total_tokens": 102616, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.0800145}
