{"id": "Q086", "question": "Which film had the biggest gap between an actor's first and second nomination, and what was that gap?", "information_need": "fact_lookup", "motivation": "bored_random", "prior_familiarity": "familiar", "scope": "multi_document", "answerable": true, "adversarial_kind": null, "required_sources": ["95th_Academy_Awards.html", "List_of_Academy_Award_records.html"], "expected_sources": ["95th_Academy_Awards.html", "List_of_Academy_Award_records.html"], "retrieved_sources": ["List_of_Academy_Award_records.html", "95th_Academy_Awards.html", "Academy_Award_for_Best_Picture.html"], "required_aspects": ["Judd Hirsch set the record for the longest gap between Oscar nominations: 42 years between his first, for Ordinary People (1980), and his second, for The Fabelmans."], "response": "The documents do not state a single film for the biggest gap between an actor’s first and second nomination. They only say that the **longest gap between first and second nomination** was **42 years**, for **Judd Hirsch**, from *Ordinary People* (1980) to *The Fabelmans* (2023) [List_of_Academy_Award_records.html].", "closed_book_response": "If you mean **Academy Award acting nominations**, the biggest gap is generally considered to be **between Katharine Hepburn’s first and second nominations** — **about 48 years**.\n\n- **First nomination:** *Morning Glory* (1933)\n- **Second nomination:** *Guess Who’s Coming to Dinner* (1967)\n\nSo the gap was **48 years**.\n\nIf you meant a different awards list or “film” in another context, tell me which one and I can narrow it down.", "correctness": "pass", "graded_correctness": "complete", "graded_correctness_score": 1.0, "covered_aspects": [1], "aspect_coverage": 1.0, "answer_relevance": "pass", "claims": [{"text": "The documents do not state a single film for the biggest gap between an actor’s first and second nomination.", "cited_source": "List_of_Academy_Award_records.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": true}, {"text": "The longest gap between first and second nomination was 42 years.", "cited_source": "List_of_Academy_Award_records.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "That 42-year gap was for Judd Hirsch.", "cited_source": "List_of_Academy_Award_records.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "Judd Hirsch’s first nomination was for Ordinary People (1980).", "cited_source": "List_of_Academy_Award_records.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}, {"text": "Judd Hirsch’s second nomination was for The Fabelmans (2023).", "cited_source": "List_of_Academy_Award_records.html", "grounded": true, "citation_supported": true, "attributable_to_retrieval": false}], "claim_count": 5, "graded_groundedness_score": 1.0, "faithfulness": "pass", "citation_support_rate": 1.0, "chunk_attribution_score": 0.2, "source_hit_at_k": 1, "source_recall_at_k": 1.0, "source_precision_at_k": 0.6666666666666666, "source_recall_strict": 1.0, "all_required_present": true, "response_quote_count": 0, "quote_fidelity_rate": null, "quote_attribution_accuracy": null, "citation_count": 1, "citation_precision": 1.0, "unsupported_citation_rate": 0.0, "refusal_outcome": "n/a", "answer_latency_seconds": 1.7767034000135027, "judge_latency_seconds": 4.844443100009812, "total_latency_seconds": 7.936581600020872, "input_tokens": 185994, "output_tokens": 510, "total_tokens": 186504, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.1417905}
